            <div xml:id="toc">

                <pb facs="0009" n="V" xml:id="pgV"/>

                <head>Contents</head>
                <list type="toc">
                    <item><ref target="#pgIII"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Preface</hi></ref></item>
                    <item><ref target="#pgVII"><hi rendition="#small-caps">List of
                            Sources</hi></ref></item>
                    <item><ref target="#pgXI"><hi rendition="#small-caps">List of Abbreviations and
                                Symbols</hi></ref></item>
                    <item><ref target="#pgXV"><hi rendition="#small-caps">List of
                        Persons</hi></ref></item>
                    <item>Part 1 <list>
                            <item><ref target="#pg1">United States national security policy: U.S.
                                    objectives and programs for national security; estimates of
                                    threats to the national security; military posture and foreign
                                    policy; organization for national security</ref></item>
                        </list></item>
                    <item>Part 2 <list>
                            <item><ref target="frus:frus1952-54v02p2/pg_845">Policy of the United
                                    States with respect to atomic energy and the regulation of
                                    armaments; President Eisenhower’s “Atoms for Peace” proposal of
                                    December 8, 1953; other foreign policy aspects of U.S.
                                    development of atomic energy</ref></item>
                            <item><ref target="frus:frus1952-54v02p2/pg_1590">Discussions with the
                                    United Kingdom and Canada regarding the danger of general war
                                    with the Soviet Union and the use of United States bases in the
                                    United Kingdom and Canada in the event of general war;
                                    arrangements for emergency use of U.S. strategic bases in
                                    foreign areas</ref></item>
                            <item><ref target="frus:frus1952-54v02p2/pg_1591">The United States
                                    foreign information program</ref></item>
                            <item><ref target="frus:frus1952-54v02p2/pg_1795">The report of the
                                    President’s Committee on International Information Activities,
                                    June 30, 1953</ref></item>
                            <item><ref target="frus:frus1952-54v02p2/pg_1903">Index</ref></item>
                        </list></item>
                </list>
